  "body": "Reported by the maintainer (2026-11-08): \"WCS is found in some of the operations as a choice in the bottom section. That origin point where motion is generated from is on a per setup basis, not per operation - the setup would define WCS, not the operation.\"\n\n## What happens\nOn an operation's **Heights** page, any height (clearance, retract, feed, top, bottom) can use the reference **Work offset**, and then shows its own **WCS** dropdown (G54-G59) - `crates/ui/src/egui_app/heights_page.rs:130-133`. The slot is stored per height in `HeightReference::WorkOffset(i)` (`crates/app/src/operation/types/height.rs`), so one operation can reference several different offsets, and different operations in one setup can disagree.\n\nUntil #196 there was no per-setup offset at all - the program's G5x was *inferred* per operation from these height references (default G54). PR #328 (#196) adds a per-setup pick (Auto or G54-G59) and refuses by name an op whose heights reference a different slot than its setup's pick - so the per-height dropdown is now a way to build a document the post refuses.\n\n## What it should be\nThe work offset is a property of the **setup** (it says where program zero is for every operation in it). A height that references the work offset should mean \"the work offset of this operation's setup\" - no slot choice on the operation.\n\n## Done means\n- The Heights page's **Work offset** reference shows no WCS dropdown; it reads (and shows, read-only) the setup's offset, with a pointer to change it on the Setups page.\n- `HeightReference::WorkOffset` stops carrying its own slot (or the slot is ignored and resolved from the setup), through a project-file migration: existing documents whose heights named a slot get that slot moved onto their setup's work offset when the whole setup agreed, and are refused by name (with the conflicting ops listed) when its ops named different slots - never silently re-pointed.\n- Posting, generation and the setup sheet read the offset only from the setup (`wcs_slot`, #328).\n- Tests: the Heights page shows no per-height WCS choice; an old project with per-height slots migrates (agreeing case) or is refused by name (conflicting case); undo of the setup's offset pick moves every height reference with it; goldens unchanged for documents that used one slot.\n\nDepends on #196 / PR #328 (per-setup work offset). Related: #326 (part alignment to the setup frame), #315.\n",
